* **Matheieu functions** Other Expressions for the Radial Functions (Valid Over More Limited Regions)
* 20.6.12 \[Me_{2^{q}}^{(p)}(z,q) = [ee_{2r}(0,q)]^{-1}\sum\limits_{k=0}^{n}(-1)^{k+r}A_{2k}^{2r}(q)Z_{2 k}^{i(p)}(2\sqrt{q}\;\cosh z)\] \[Mc_{4r+1}^{i(p)}(z,q) = [ee_{2r+1}(0,q)]^{-1}\sum\limits_{k=0}^{n}(-1)^{k+r}A_{2k+1}^{2r+1} (q)Z_{2k+1}^{i(p)}(2\sqrt{q}\;\cosh z)\]
* 20.6.13 \[M_{8z^{ij}}^{(p)}(z,q) = [se_{2r}^{e}(0,q)]^{-1}\tanh\;z\sum\limits_{k=1}^{n}(-1)^{k+r}2kB_{2 i}^{2r}(q)Z_{2 k}^{i(p)}(2\sqrt{q}\;\cosh z)\] \[M_{8z^{ij}+1}^{i(p)}(z,q) = [se_{2r+1}^{e}(0,q)]^{-1}\tanh\;z\sum\limits_{k=0}^{n}(-1)^{k+r}(2k +1)B_{2i+1}^{2r+1}(q)Z_{2k+1}^{i(p)}(2\sqrt{q}\;\cosh z)\]

Valid for \(\mathscr{R}z\)>0, \(|\cosh z|\)>1; if \(j\)=1, valid for all \(z\). They agree with 20.6.7-20.6.10 if the Bessel functions \(Y_{m}(2q^{k}\cosh z)\) are made single-valued in a suitable way. For example, let

\[Y_{m}(u) = \frac{2}{\pi}\left(\ln u\right)J_{m}(u) + \phi(u)\]

where \(\phi(u)\) is single-valued for all finite values of \(u\). With \(u\)=2\(q^{k}\) cosh \(z\), define

* 20.6.14 In \((2q^{k}\cosh z)\)=\(\ln 2q^{k}\)+\(z\)+\(\ln\)\(\frac{1}{2}(1\)+\(e^{-u})\)\(-\frac{\pi}{2}\leq\)arg \(1(1\)+\(e^{-u})\)\(\leq\)\(\frac{\pi}{2}\). (If \(q\) is not positive, the phase of \(\ln 2q^{k}\) must also be specified, although this specification will not affect continuity with respect to \(z\). If \(Y_{m}(u)\) is defined from some other expression, the definition must be compatible with 20.6.14.)

